Author:     Ben Campbell <benc@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Wed Jun 4 18:28:32 2025 +0200
Commit:     Ben Campbell <benc@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Wed Jun 4 18:28:32 2025 +0200

    Bug 1952094 - Add nsIMsgDatabase.attachHdr() to allow separation of detached and live nsIMsgHdr objects. r=darktrojan,mkmelin


    The legacy (mork) DB code makes no real distinction between nsIMsgDBHdr
    objects which are "detached" (rows created in the DB, but not attached to
    the messages table) and "live" (attached to the messages table).
    Sqlite doesn't really support detached rows, so this patch provides
    detached nsIMsgDBHdr objects as a completely separate implementation,
    which holds their own data rather than relying on a detached row in the
    the database.
    It also adds a new method, attachHdr() which attaches a detached hdr
    to the messages table and returns a 'live' nsIMsgDBHdr object.
    For the legacy code, the detached and live objects are the same object,
    but for the new sqlite-based globaldb, they are separate.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D250889

